1
00:07:03,333 --> 00:07:09,333
In our darkest hour, a hero will rise.

2
00:14:06,666 --> 00:14:12,666
Wolf Hound is a war, action film directed by Michael B. Chait.

3
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Inspired by the real-life German special operations unit KG 200 that shot down, repaired, and flew Allied aircraft as Trojan horses, "Wolf Hound"
takes place in 1944 German-occupied France and follows the daring exploits of Jewish-American fighter pilot Captain David Holden.

4
00:28:13,333 --> 00:28:19,333
Ambushed behind enemy lines, Holden must rescue a captured B-17 Flying Fortress crew, evade a ruthless enemy
stalking him at every turn, and foil a plot that could completely alter the outcome of World War II.

5
00:35:16,666 --> 00:35:22,666
Captain David Holden, played by James Maslow.

6
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:26,000
Major Erich Roth, played by Trevor Donovan.

7
00:49:23,333 --> 00:49:29,333
Colonel Krieger, played by John Turk.

8
00:56:26,666 --> 00:56:32,666
Captain Rolf Werner, played by Michael Wayne Foster.

9
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:36,000
Captain Heinrich Roth, played by Ronald Woodhead.

10
01:10:33,333 --> 01:10:39,333
Captain Richard Thompson, played by Michael Parrish.

11
01:17:36,666 --> 01:17:42,666
Huckleberry "Huck" Hound is a fictional cartoon character, a
blue dog who speaks with a North Carolina accent.

12
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:46,000
He first appeared in the series The Huckleberry Hound Show.

13
01:31:43,333 --> 01:31:49,333
The cartoon was one of six TV shows to win an Emmy Award in 1960 as a Primetime Emmy Award for
Outstanding Children's Program; the first animated series to receive such an award.

14
01:38:46,666 --> 01:38:52,666
In most of his cartoons he has different jobs, with results that backfire, yet
usually coming out on top, either through slow persistence or sheer luck.

15
01:45:50,000 --> 01:45:56,000
He has been a Roman gladiator, a medieval knight, a
dogcatcher, a policeman and a rocket scientist.

16
01:52:53,333 --> 01:52:59,333
He also appears in futuristic cartoons, as an intergalactic space
policeman, alongside other Hanna-Barbera characters.

17
01:59:56,666 --> 02:00:02,666
His off-key and inaccurate rendition of "Oh My Darling,
Clementine" was often used as a running gag.
